  "name": "KinaseMD 2.0",
  "description": "A public human kinase database linking cancer-associated somatic mutations and structural annotations to cell-line inhibitor response, phosphorylation evidence, and candidate phosphosites for experimental follow-up. The published 2.0 release covers 547 human protein kinases and 422,244 cell-line drug-response measurements.",
